{
    "//": [
        "HiDPI variants of the system's art, for tools/hidpi-art.py: name@2x.png and name@3x.png beside each name.png.",
        "The top level is the shell's Open webOS art (shell/assets/openwebos); `sets` are the Phoenix apps' kit and",
        "luna-systemui's (`art`: the 1x files; `out`: where the variants go, when not beside them).",
        "original: a variant copied from art Open webOS / Enyo already ship at that size (from: its path in that",
        "  repository, checked out under --ref; repo: where it is).",
        "upscale: art shipped at 1x only, enlarged to `factors` (default above), corrected so it scales back down to",
        "  the 1x art (back-projection). `method`: model (default; Real-ESRGAN, the model below, 4x: icons, glyphs,",
        "  pictures), smooth (bicubic: gradients, shadows, masks, panels, key tiles; no grain), copy (the variants of",
        "  `from`, the same picture elsewhere in the repository). `tiles`: [columns, rows] of a sprite sheet, enlarged",
        "  one cell at a time so the cells do not bleed into each other. `wrap`: x, y or xy for art the shell tiles.",
        "  `from` (model, smooth): enlarge that variant (an original, beside the others) instead of the 1x art.",
        "derived: variants another tool writes (checked here). skip: left at 1x, each with its reason.",
        "css: stylesheets whose url()s of art with variants must be image sets of them all. overlay-css: a stylesheet",
        "  written for a submodule's pages, repeating its image rules as image sets.",
        "See docs/spec/hidpi-art.md and shell/assets/openwebos/PROVENANCE.md."
    ],
